## The changelog gate

Every publishing repo should fail its own stable release when `CHANGELOG.md` has no section
for the version being cut. `SpiralGenesis` established this and `Keyframe` mirrors it:

* a **stable** tag with no `## [X.Y.Z]` section fails the release with an actionable message
* a **pre-release** tag may ship without one - alphas move faster than the changelog
* release notes are taken from the matching section, with generated notes appended

The failure it prevents is silent: a stable release tagged while `CHANGELOG.md` still says
only `[Unreleased]` publishes with no record of what changed and nobody notices.
